{
  "title": "agent.completions.message.AssistantToolCallExpression",
  "description": "A function call expression.",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "function": {
      "description": "The function expression.

A value that can be either a literal or an expression.

This allows Function definitions to mix static values with dynamic
expressions. During compilation, expressions are evaluated while
literal values pass through unchanged.

# Example

Literal value:
```json
"hello world"
```

JMESPath expression:
```json
{"$jmespath": "input.greeting"}
```

Starlark expression:
```json
{"$starlark": "input['greeting']"}
```",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "Expression",
          "description": "An expression (JMESPath or Starlark) to evaluate.",
          "$ref": "functions.expression.Expression"
        },
        {
          "title": "Value",
          "description": "A literal value.",
          "$ref": "agent.completions.message.AssistantToolCallFunctionExpression"
        }
      ]
    },
    "id": {
      "description": "The tool call ID expression.

A value that can be either a literal or an expression.

This allows Function definitions to mix static values with dynamic
expressions. During compilation, expressions are evaluated while
literal values pass through unchanged.

# Example

Literal value:
```json
"hello world"
```

JMESPath expression:
```json
{"$jmespath": "input.greeting"}
```

Starlark expression:
```json
{"$starlark": "input['greeting']"}
```",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "title": "Expression",
          "description": "An expression (JMESPath or Starlark) to evaluate.",
          "$ref": "functions.expression.Expression"
        },
        {
          "title": "Value",
          "description": "A literal value.",
          "type": "string"
        }
      ]
    },
    "type": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "function"
      ]
    }
  }
}

{
  "title": "agent.completions.message.File",
  "description": "A file attachment for multimodal input.",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "file_data": {
      "description": "Base64-encoded file data.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "omitempty": true
    },
    "file_id": {
      "description": "The ID of a previously uploaded file.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "omitempty": true
    },
    "file_url": {
      "description": "A URL to fetch the file from.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "omitempty": true
    },
    "filename": {
      "description": "The filename for display purposes.",
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "omitempty": true
    }
  }
}
